IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sca-nouns`

-- State Courts Act 1970 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition -- LAYER 1, PART 2: CONSTITUTION (ss 3 to 8).
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Act itself gives; NOTHING means the Act does not answer on
-- these facts.  Every branch that says no carries a FALSE-kind comment, every NOTHING a NOTHING-kind comment (NOTES.md).

§ `Section 3 -- the State Courts`

-- src:240 | 3.—(1) There are within Singapore the following subordinate
-- src:241 | courts called the State Courts:
-- src:243 | (a) District Courts;
-- src:245 | (b) Magistrates’ Courts;
-- src:247 | (c) Coroners’ Courts;
-- src:249 | (d) Small Claims Tribunals;
-- src:251 | (e) Employment Claims Tribunals.
@ref s 3(1)(a) to (e) (src:240-251)
GIVEN court IS A `Court or tribunal`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(1) the court is one of the State Courts` MEANS
    CONSIDER court
    WHEN `District Court` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Magistrate's Court` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Coroner's Court` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Small Claims Tribunal` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Employment Claims Tribunal` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "the following subordinate courts called the State Courts" lists five courts and does not close the list with "only"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:255 | (1A) The District Courts and Magistrates’ Courts have the
-- src:256 | jurisdiction conferred by this Act and any other written law.
@ref s 3(1A) (src:255-256)
GIVEN court IS A `Court or tribunal`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(1A) the court has the jurisdiction conferred by this Act and any other written law` MEANS
    CONSIDER court
    WHEN `District Court` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Magistrate's Court` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about "The District Courts and Magistrates’ Courts" and says nothing of any other court
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:260 | (2) The Small Claims Tribunals have the jurisdiction conferred by
-- src:261 | the Small Claims Tribunals Act 1984 and any other written law.
@ref s 3(2) (src:260-261)
GIVEN court IS A `Court or tribunal`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(2) the court has the jurisdiction conferred by the Small Claims Tribunals Act 1984 and any other written law` MEANS
    CONSIDER court
    WHEN `Small Claims Tribunal` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about "The Small Claims Tribunals" and says nothing of any other court
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:268 | (4) The Coroners’ Courts have the jurisdiction that is conferred by
-- src:269 | the Coroners Act 2010 and any other written law.
@ref s 3(4) (src:268-269)
GIVEN court IS A `Court or tribunal`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(4) the court has the jurisdiction conferred by the Coroners Act 2010 and any other written law` MEANS
    CONSIDER court
    WHEN `Coroner's Court` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about "The Coroners’ Courts" and says nothing of any other court
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:273 | (5) The Employment Claims Tribunals have the jurisdiction that is
-- src:274 | conferred by the Employment Claims Act 2016 and any other written
-- src:275 | law.
@ref s 3(5) (src:273-275)
GIVEN court IS A `Court or tribunal`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(5) the court has the jurisdiction conferred by the Employment Claims Act 2016 and any other written law` MEANS
    CONSIDER court
    WHEN `Employment Claims Tribunal` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about "The Employment Claims Tribunals" and says nothing of any other court
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `Sections 4 to 6 -- constitution, seals and process`

-- src:281 | 4. The President may constitute under appropriate names so many
-- src:282 | State Courts as the President thinks fit.
@ref s 4 (src:281-282)
GIVEN `the President constituted the court under an appropriate name` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4 the State Court is constituted by the President under an appropriate name` MEANS
    IF `the President constituted the court under an appropriate name`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): section 4 gives the President a power and does not say how else a State Court may come to be constituted
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:292 | 5. The State Courts are to have and use as occasion may require a
-- src:293 | seal or seals of such nature as the Chief Justice may, by notification in
-- src:294 | the Gazette, prescribe.
@ref s 5 (src:292-294)
GIVEN `the seal is of the nature the Chief Justice prescribed by notification in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5 the State Courts have and use a seal of the nature the Chief Justice has prescribed as the section requires` MEANS
    IF `the seal is of the nature the Chief Justice prescribed by notification in the Gazette`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "are to have and use ... a seal" is a bare requirement (QB) and the Act does not say what follows when the seal is of another nature
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:300 | 6. Subject to Rules of Court, all writs, summonses, warrants,
-- src:301 | orders, notices and other mandatory processes issued by the State
-- src:302 | Courts must be signed by a judicial officer and must bear the seal of
-- src:303 | the court issuing the same.
@ref s 6 (src:300-303)
GIVEN `a judicial officer signed it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it bears the seal of the court issuing it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Rules of Court provide otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 6 the process of the State Courts is signed by a judicial officer and bears the seal of the court as the section requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Subject to Rules of Court" leaves the position to Rules of Court that are not among the sources
        IF `the Rules of Court provide otherwise` THEN NOTHING
        IF `a judicial officer signed it` AND `it bears the seal of the court issuing it` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "must be signed ... and must bear the seal" is a bare "must" (QB); the Act does not say here what follows when the process is not signed or not sealed
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

@ref s 6 (src:300-303)
-- The duty in s 6 as a regulative rule: a judicial officer must sign the process and it must bear the seal.
-- The Act states no time limit and no consequence, so none is written (the defaults of the language apply).
`s 6 duty: a judicial officer must sign the process and the process must bear the seal` MEANS
    PARTY `A judicial officer`
    MUST `sign the process and bear the seal of the court`

§ `Section 6A -- sittings of State Courts`

-- src:309 | 6A.—(1) Subject to subsection (2), every State Court is to sit on
-- src:310 | every day of the year except on Saturdays, Sundays and public
-- src:311 | holidays.
@ref s 6A(1) (src:309-311)
GIVEN day IS A `Kind of day`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 6A(1) the State Court is to sit on the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER day
    WHEN `Ordinary day` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "every State Court is to sit on every day of the year except on Saturdays, Sundays and public holidays"
    WHEN Saturday THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "every State Court is to sit on every day of the year except on Saturdays, Sundays and public holidays"
    WHEN Sunday THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "every State Court is to sit on every day of the year except on Saturdays, Sundays and public holidays"
    WHEN `Public holiday` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (1) is "Subject to subsection (2)", and subsection (2) speaks of "a vacation authorised under section 61" as a time when a judicial officer needs a direction to sit; (1) itself does not except vacations
    WHEN `Day in a vacation authorised under section 61` THEN NOTHING

-- src:315 | (2) Despite subsection (1), a judicial officer may lawfully sit on a
-- src:316 | Saturday, Sunday or public holiday or during a vacation authorised
-- src:317 | under section 61 if —
-- src:322 | (a) the Presiding Judge of the State Courts, with the
-- src:323 | concurrence of the Chief Justice, has directed the judicial
-- src:324 | officer to sit on that day or during that vacation; or
-- src:326 | (b) in the opinion of the judicial officer, the business to be
-- src:327 | despatched is extremely urgent.
@ref s 6A(2)(a) and (b) (src:315-327)
GIVEN day IS A `Kind of day`
      `the Presiding Judge, with the concurrence of the Chief Justice, has directed the judicial officer to sit on that day or during that vacation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the opinion of the judicial officer the business to be despatched is extremely urgent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 6A(2) the judicial officer may lawfully sit on the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER day
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is for "a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday or during a vacation authorised under section 61"; on an ordinary day subsection (1) governs
    WHEN `Ordinary day` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the Presiding Judge, with the concurrence of the Chief Justice, has directed the judicial officer to sit on that day or during that vacation` OR `in the opinion of the judicial officer the business to be despatched is extremely urgent`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may lawfully sit ... if (a) ... or (b) ..." (a failed "if" is taken as the text's no: marginal reading (a))
             JUST FALSE

-- src:331 | (3) Every State Court is to sit at such times and at such places as the
-- src:332 | Chief Justice may from time to time appoint.
@ref s 6A(3) (src:331-332)
GIVEN `it sits at the time and place the Chief Justice appointed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 6A(3) the State Court sits at the time and place the Chief Justice has appointed as the section requires` MEANS
    IF `it sits at the time and place the Chief Justice appointed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "is to sit at such times and at such places as the Chief Justice may ... appoint" is a bare requirement (QB); the Act does not say what follows when it sits elsewhere
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 7 -- sittings in private, etc.`

-- src:340 | 7.—(1) The place in which any State Court is held is deemed an
-- src:341 | open and public court to which the public generally may have access.
@ref s 7(1) (src:340-341)
GIVEN `it is the place in which a State Court is held` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(1) the place is deemed an open and public court to which the public may have access` MEANS
    IF `it is the place in which a State Court is held`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the deeming is of "The place in which any State Court is held" and says nothing of another place
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:345 | (2) A State Court has the power to hear any matter or proceeding or
-- src:346 | any part thereof in private if the court is satisfied that it is expedient in
-- src:347 | the interests of justice, public safety, public security or propriety, the
-- src:348 | national interest or national security of Singapore, or for other
-- src:349 | sufficient reason to do so.
@ref s 7(2) (src:345-349)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that it is expedient in the interests of justice, public safety, public security or propriety, the national interest or national security, or for other sufficient reason` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(2) the State Court has power to hear the matter or part of it in private` MEANS
    IF `the court is satisfied that it is expedient in the interests of justice, public safety, public security or propriety, the national interest or national security, or for other sufficient reason`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "has the power to hear ... in private if the court is satisfied" (a failed "if" is taken as the text's no: marginal reading (a))
         JUST FALSE

-- src:355 | (2AA) Any application for a matter or proceeding to be held in
-- src:356 | private, on the grounds that it is expedient in the national interest or
-- src:357 | national security of Singapore to do so, is to be heard in private.
@ref s 7(2AA) (src:355-357)
GIVEN `the application is on the grounds that it is expedient in the national interest or national security of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(2AA) the application is to be heard in private` MEANS
    IF `the application is on the grounds that it is expedient in the national interest or national security of Singapore`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the requirement is for "Any application ... on the grounds that it is expedient in the national interest or national security"; other applications are governed by subsection (2)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:361 | (2AB) A State Court has the power to hear any application
-- src:362 | mentioned in subsection (2AA), or any part of such an application,
-- src:363 | otherwise than in private, if the court is satisfied that —
-- src:365 | (a) it is expedient in the interests of justice to hear the
-- src:366 | application or part of the application otherwise than in
-- src:367 | private; and
-- src:369 | (b) it is not prejudicial to the national interest or national
-- src:370 | security of Singapore to hear the application or part of the
-- src:371 | application otherwise than in private.
@ref s 7(2AB)(a) and (b) (src:361-371)
GIVEN `it is expedient in the interests of justice to hear the application or part of it otherwise than in private` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is not prejudicial to the national interest or national security to hear the application or part of it otherwise than in private` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(2AB) the State Court has power to hear the subsection (2AA) application otherwise than in private` MEANS
    IF `it is expedient in the interests of justice to hear the application or part of it otherwise than in private` AND `it is not prejudicial to the national interest or national security to hear the application or part of it otherwise than in private`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "has the power ... if the court is satisfied that — (a) ...; and (b) ..." (a failed "if" is taken as the text's no: marginal reading (a))
         JUST FALSE

-- src:378 | (2A) A State Court may, in any matter or proceeding or any part
-- src:379 | thereof tried or held or to be tried or held before it, if satisfied that it is
-- src:380 | expedient in the interests of justice, public safety, public security or
-- src:381 | propriety, the national interest or national security of Singapore, or
-- src:382 | for other sufficient reason to do so, order that —
-- src:384 | (a) the name, address or photograph of any witness;
-- src:388 | (b) any evidence or any other thing likely to lead to the
-- src:389 | identification of such witness by a person other than the
-- src:390 | party to that matter or proceeding; or
-- src:394 | (c) any information that, if disclosed, may be prejudicial to the
-- src:395 | national interest or national security of Singapore,
-- src:397 | which is contained in any court document intended to be produced
-- src:398 | before the court, be removed or be sufficiently redacted.
@ref s 7(2A)(a) to (c) (src:378-398)
GIVEN material IS A `Material in a court document`
      `the court is satisfied that it is expedient in the interests of justice, public safety, public security or propriety, the national interest or national security, or for other sufficient reason` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(2A) the State Court may order the material to be removed or sufficiently redacted` MEANS
    CONSIDER material
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power covers the three kinds of material in paragraphs (a) to (c) of a court document intended to be produced before the court
    WHEN `Other material` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the court is satisfied that it is expedient in the interests of justice, public safety, public security or propriety, the national interest or national security, or for other sufficient reason`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A State Court may ... if satisfied that it is expedient ... order that" (a failed "if" is taken as the text's no: marginal reading (a))
             JUST FALSE

-- src:404 | (3) A State Court may at any time order that no person is to —
-- src:406 | (a) publish the name, address or photograph of any witness in
-- src:407 | any matter or proceeding or any part thereof tried or held or
-- src:408 | to be tried or held before it, or any evidence or any other
-- src:409 | thing likely to lead to the identification of any such
-- src:410 | witness;
-- src:414 | (b) do any other act which is likely to lead to the identification
-- src:415 | of any witness mentioned in paragraph (a); or
-- src:421 | (c) publish any information relating to any matter or
-- src:422 | proceeding before the court that, if disclosed, may be
-- src:423 | prejudicial to the national interest or national security of
-- src:424 | Singapore.
@ref s 7(3)(a) to (c) (src:404-424)
GIVEN act IS AN `Act that an order may forbid`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(3) the State Court may at any time order that no person is to do the act` MEANS
    CONSIDER act
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): section 7(3) names three kinds of act and does not say that a State Court may order nothing else
    WHEN `Another act` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:428 | (4) Any person who acts in contravention of any order under
-- src:429 | subsection (2A) or (3) shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable
-- src:434 | on conviction to a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a
-- src:435 | term not exceeding 12 months or to both.
@ref s 7(4) (src:428-435)
GIVEN `the person acted in contravention of an order under subsection (2A) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(4) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the person acted in contravention of an order under subsection (2A) or (3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person who acts in contravention of any order under subsection (2A) or (3)" says nothing of a person who did not
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref s 7(4) (src:428-435)
GIVEN fine IS A NUMBER
      `months of imprisonment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(4) the punishment is within the greatest the offence allows` MEANS
    IF fine AT MOST 5_000 AND `months of imprisonment` AT MOST 12
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or to both"
         JUST FALSE

@ref s 7(4) (src:428-435)
-- The prohibition in s 7(4) as a regulative rule: any person shall not act in contravention of an order under s 7(2A) or (3).
-- The Act states no time limit; the consequence (offence and punishment) is s 7(4) itself and is not a state of this rule.
`s 7(4) duty: any person shall not contravene an order under section 7(2A) or 7(3)` MEANS
    PARTY `Any person`
    SHANT `contravene an order under section 7(2A) or 7(3)`

-- src:439 | (5) A State Court that hears the whole or any part of any matter or
-- src:440 | proceeding in private may, in its discretion, permit any of the
-- src:441 | following individuals to be present in the courtroom while that matter
-- src:442 | or proceeding is heard in private:
-- src:444 | (a) any journalist who reports news for a newspaper or a
-- src:445 | broadcasting service;
-- src:447 | (b) any individual whom the court determines has a sufficient
-- src:448 | interest in that matter or proceeding;
-- src:450 | (c) any other individual that the court specifies in any
-- src:451 | particular case.
@ref s 7(5)(a) to (c) (src:439-451)
GIVEN `the court heard the whole or part of the matter or proceeding in private` IS A BOOLEAN
      individual IS AN `Individual who might be present`
      `the court, in its discretion, has permitted the individual to be present` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(5) the individual may be present in the courtroom while the matter is heard in private` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection is about "A State Court that hears the whole or any part of any matter or proceeding in private"
        IF NOT (`the court heard the whole or part of the matter or proceeding in private`) THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the subsection names three kinds of individual and does not say that the court may permit no one else
        IF individual EQUALS `Anyone else` THEN NOTHING
        IF `the court, in its discretion, has permitted the individual to be present` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the court "may, in its discretion, permit"; the subsection does not say that an individual the court has not permitted may not be present
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:457 | (6) For the purposes of subsection (2), the matters that a State Court
-- src:458 | may consider, when deciding whether it is expedient in the interests
