-- src:484 | (e) whether any information that may be disclosed during the
-- src:485 | hearing of that matter or proceeding will be prejudicial to
-- src:486 | the interests of Singapore.
@ref s 7(6)(a) to (e) (src:457-486)
GIVEN matter IS A `Matter the court may consider`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(6) the matter is one the State Court may consider in deciding whether to hear the matter in private` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "the matters that a State Court may consider ... include the following matters" does not close the list
    WHEN `Another matter` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

