§ `Section 8 -- hearings through electronic means of communication`

-- src:505 | 8.—(1) Without limiting section 7, a State Court may conduct the
-- src:506 | hearing of any matter or proceeding (other than a matter or
-- src:507 | proceeding prescribed by the Rules of Court or the Criminal
-- src:508 | Procedure Rules) through a live video link, a live television link, a
-- src:509 | live audio link or any other electronic means of communication
-- src:510 | approved by the Chief Justice.
@ref s 8(1) (src:505-510)
GIVEN `the matter is one prescribed by the Rules of Court or the Criminal Procedure Rules` IS A BOOLEAN
      means IS A `Means of hearing`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(1) the State Court may conduct the hearing through the means` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(other than a matter or proceeding prescribed by the Rules of Court or the Criminal Procedure Rules)" takes those matters out of the grant (QE: a limit on a grant, so NOTHING for them)
        IF `the matter is one prescribed by the Rules of Court or the Criminal Procedure Rules` THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is of "any other electronic means of communication approved by the Chief Justice"; a means he has not approved is outside it
        IF means EQUALS `Another electronic means of communication not approved by the Chief Justice` THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:514 | (2) Subsection (1) does not affect the operation of section 26A of
-- src:515 | the Administration of Justice (Protection) Act 2016, section 62A of
-- src:516 | the Evidence Act 1893 and section 281 of the Criminal Procedure
-- src:517 | Code 2010.
@ref s 8(2) (src:514-517)
GIVEN provision IS A `Provision of another Act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(2) subsection (1) affects the operation of the provision` MEANS
    CONSIDER provision
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not affect the operation of section 26A of the Administration of Justice (Protection) Act 2016, section 62A of the Evidence Act 1893 and section 281 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010"
    WHEN `Section 26A of the Administration of Justice (Protection) Act 2016` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not affect the operation of section 26A of the Administration of Justice (Protection) Act 2016, section 62A of the Evidence Act 1893 and section 281 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010"
    WHEN `Section 62A of the Evidence Act 1893` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not affect the operation of section 26A of the Administration of Justice (Protection) Act 2016, section 62A of the Evidence Act 1893 and section 281 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010"
    WHEN `Section 281 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010` THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection names three provisions and does not say whether subsection (1) affects any other
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:523 | (3) A State Court must not conduct any part of a hearing of a matter
-- src:524 | through a live audio link only, without an accompanying live video
-- src:525 | link or live television link —
-- src:527 | (a) where oral evidence is given during that part of the hearing
-- src:528 | (including in a trial of an offence) in a criminal proceeding;
-- src:530 | (b) where oral evidence is given during that part of the hearing
-- src:531 | (including in a trial of an action) in a civil proceeding,
-- src:532 | unless all the parties consent; or
-- src:537 | (c) where the matter is prescribed by the Rules of Court or the
-- src:538 | Criminal Procedure Rules.
@ref s 8(3)(a) to (c) (src:523-538)
GIVEN `the part of the hearing is in a criminal proceeding and oral evidence is given during it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the part of the hearing is in a civil proceeding and oral evidence is given during it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all the parties consent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is prescribed by the Rules of Court or the Criminal Procedure Rules` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(3) the State Court may conduct the part of the hearing through a live audio link only` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A State Court must not conduct any part of a hearing of a matter through a live audio link only ... (a) where oral evidence is given ... in a criminal proceeding"
        IF `the part of the hearing is in a criminal proceeding and oral evidence is given during it` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not ... (b) where oral evidence is given ... in a civil proceeding, unless all the parties consent"
        IF `the part of the hearing is in a civil proceeding and oral evidence is given during it` AND NOT (`all the parties consent`) THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not ... (c) where the matter is prescribed by the Rules of Court or the Criminal Procedure Rules"
        IF `the matter is prescribed by the Rules of Court or the Criminal Procedure Rules` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless all the parties consent" lifts the bar in paragraph (b) and a lifted bar grants nothing (QA: the permission question answers NOTHING); where no paragraph applies, subsection (3) is silent and section 8(1) is the grant
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

@ref s 8(3)(a) to (c) (src:523-538)
GIVEN `the part of the hearing is in a criminal proceeding and oral evidence is given during it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the part of the hearing is in a civil proceeding and oral evidence is given during it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all the parties consent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is prescribed by the Rules of Court or the Criminal Procedure Rules` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(3) the bar on a live audio link only applies to the part of the hearing` MEANS
    IF `the part of the hearing is in a criminal proceeding and oral evidence is given during it`
       OR (`the part of the hearing is in a civil proceeding and oral evidence is given during it` AND NOT (`all the parties consent`))
       OR `the matter is prescribed by the Rules of Court or the Criminal Procedure Rules`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the bar applies only "(a) where oral evidence is given ... in a criminal proceeding; (b) where oral evidence is given ... in a civil proceeding, unless all the parties consent; or (c) where the matter is prescribed" (a "where" that is not met answers JUST FALSE, ruling of 2026-11-05; "unless" lifts the bar in (b))
         JUST FALSE

@ref s 8(3) (src:523-538)
-- The prohibition in s 8(3) as a regulative rule: a State Court shall not conduct a part of a hearing through a live audio link only in the cases s 8(3) lists.
`s 8(3) duty: a State Court shall not conduct a part of a hearing through a live audio link only` MEANS
    PARTY `A State Court`
    SHANT `conduct a part of a hearing through a live audio link only`

-- src:542 | (4) For the purposes of subsection (3), a court is not considered to
-- src:543 | have conducted a part of a hearing of a matter through a live audio
-- src:544 | link only and without an accompanying live video link or live
-- src:545 | television link, by reason only of a temporary disruption in the
-- src:546 | accompanying live video link or live television link that was
-- src:547 | insignificant and which did not affect the court’s duty to conduct
-- src:548 | proceedings fairly.
@ref s 8(4) (src:542-548)
GIVEN `there was a temporary disruption in the accompanying live video link or live television link` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disruption was insignificant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disruption did not affect the court's duty to conduct proceedings fairly` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(4) the court is considered to have conducted the part of the hearing through a live audio link only` MEANS
    IF `there was a temporary disruption in the accompanying live video link or live television link` AND `the disruption was insignificant` AND `the disruption did not affect the court's duty to conduct proceedings fairly`
    THEN -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a court is not considered to have conducted a part of a hearing ... through a live audio link only ... by reason only of a temporary disruption ... that was insignificant and which did not affect the court’s duty to conduct proceedings fairly"
         JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the "not considered" is "by reason only of" such a disruption; on other facts subsection (4) is silent
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:552 | (5) A State Court must not conduct a hearing of a matter or
-- src:553 | proceeding in the manner provided under subsection (1), if to do so
-- src:554 | would be inconsistent with the court’s duty to ensure that the hearing
-- src:555 | is conducted fairly to all parties.
@ref s 8(5) (src:552-555)
GIVEN `to conduct the hearing in the manner provided under subsection (1) would be inconsistent with the court's duty to ensure that the hearing is conducted fairly to all parties` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(5) the State Court may conduct the hearing in the manner provided under subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF `to conduct the hearing in the manner provided under subsection (1) would be inconsistent with the court's duty to ensure that the hearing is conducted fairly to all parties`
    THEN -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A State Court must not conduct a hearing of a matter or proceeding in the manner provided under subsection (1), if to do so would be inconsistent with the court’s duty to ensure that the hearing is conducted fairly to all parties"
         JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar applies "if" the hearing would be unfair; where it would not, subsection (5) grants nothing and section 8(1) is the grant
    ELSE NOTHING

